.TH SIGN-APK-REPO 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sign-apk-repo \- repository publication and signing gate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sign-apk-repo
.RB [ --full-audit ]
.RI [ PKG ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sign-apk-repo
publishes ready transactions into the generation repositories: it
validates transaction integrity (manifests, seeds, canonical
constructors, checksums), retires pure-rebuild conflicts
automatically, gates file ownership and Unix identities against the
indexed
.I repository.db
(fast path: staged set only), regenerates and signs both indexes,
installs everything atomically, and renames transactions published.
.PP
Bare runs are the fast production path.
.B --full-audit
is the deliberate expensive reconstruction and verification path
(census, ledger reconcile, tombstone verification -- tombstones are
never destroyed from current-only state). A missing or unusable
database refuses with a migration pointer; it is never silently
recreated (see
.BR saphira-repo-migrate (8)).
Positional arguments are target filters only; they never select the
gate algorithm. Must be run as root; use sudo explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --full-audit
Reconstruct and verify instead of fast-gating.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /out/stage4/incoming/
Staging transactions
.RI ( *-ready ,
.IR *-published ).
.TP
.I /out/stage4/packages/<generation>/$ARCH/repository.db
The gated metadata both modes trust or rebuild.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Published (or nothing left after automatic retirement).
.TP
.B 1
Gate refusal or publication failure; nothing partial is left behind.
.TP
.B 2
Database missing or unusable: run the named migration or reconcile.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
sudo sign-apk-repo
.br
sudo sign-apk-repo --full-audit
.RE
